    "body": "Great on any Friday: AAWireless Two - Android Auto Wireless Adapter\n2028 Subaru Crosstrek Receives a Mid-Cycle Refresh in CGI, Complete With Fresh Colors Inside-Out\n12 photos\nPhoto: AutoYa Interior / YouTube\nThe Japanese automaker Subaru has done a few things lately – they just launched the all-new E-Outback (aka Trailseeker in America) in the United Kingdom, costing no less than $65k at the current exchange rate. For Japan, they announced the US-produced Ascent Touring is going to the home market as a special edition, and there was also commotion in the sporty department.\nOver there, the fans got a reminder from Subaru that it can do funky things, so the new TY85 manual-equipped WRX STI Sport R recorded more than 1,000 pre-orders at home in Japan in just two days. Sadly, it’s not even a full-blown STI anymore – only looks and acts like one without the extra oomph, actually.\nAnyway, back to America, Subaru had a great month of October this year - Subaru of America reported sales were up by six percent to 54k units, with the Crosstrek compact CUV taking the first spot, followed by the larger Forester, both reaching their best-ever sales for the month of October of any year. Year-to-date, Subaru is on the right track to recover from the initial slump, and now it’s down less than one percent compared to last year.\nBut obviously they need to continue with the good trend in order to come out with a positive result by the end of the year. The Legacy, for example, is on its way out of the model range, and the electric Solterra is down more than 42% while the Impreza has also bottomed out by 41%. No worries, as the rumor mill and the members of the imaginative guild of digital car content creators are ready to give a helping hand.\nMore precisely, the good folks over at the \" AutoYa \" info channel on YouTube have a satellite venue dubbed \" AutoYa Interior, \" which is where all the CGI Subaru action resides, and they have prepared a mid-cycle refresh for the 2028 Crosstrek, the company’s second-most popular nameplate currently.\nAccording to the channel’s host, in 2027 we might see the Subaru Crosstrek get updated for the mid-cycle refresh cycle for the 2028 model year, as the third generation was introduced during the 2024 model year in North America. It could receive new engine options, like the 2.4-liter turbo and even a PHEV option alongside the hybrid, but more importantly, it would sport various exterior and interior enhancements.\nThose include modified rear lights, a reworked grille with redesigned headlights and LED daytime running lights for the exterior, along with new alloy wheel options and possibly additional colors. The changes inside are also pretty easy to observe, at least in these renderings: Subaru could introduce a new steering wheel and a reworked cockpit for the driver.\nThe latter could get a fully digital instrument cluster along with a different infotainment screen which abandons the portrait style for a classic landscape layout and gains new functionality. Of course, the resident virtual artist didn’t miss the chance to showcase new hues, either.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2028 Subaru Crosstrek Subaru Crosstrek Subaru crosstrek compact crossover SUV CGI facelift rendering AutoYa Interior\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Porsche Took 1.5 Years to Turn a 911 GT3 Into a One-Off Tribute to the 911 GT1",
